1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,393
PC and phone memory prices were forecast to rise over 90% in three months

2
00:00:05,413 --> 00:00:08,661
Shocked by RAM prices this year?

3
00:00:08,681 --> 00:00:12,389
What AI hoovers up is HBM, next to the AI chip

4
00:00:12,409 --> 00:00:15,495
So why did PC RAM prices rise too?

5
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:19,236
HBM needs about three times the wafers for the same amount

6
00:00:19,256 --> 00:00:21,476
That's Micron's own ratio

7
00:00:21,496 --> 00:00:26,428
A bakery using triple flour for cakes runs short of bread, so bread gets pricier

8
00:00:26,448 --> 00:00:28,386
Memory fabs are the same

9
00:00:28,406 --> 00:00:32,153
Samsung sells more of this memory than anyone

10
00:00:32,173 --> 00:00:35,299
It earned 107 trillion won in Q3 alone

11
00:00:35,319 --> 00:00:43,082
Gartner sees DRAM prices falling from late 2027; Micron says the 2028 shortage will be worse than this year's

12
00:00:43,102 --> 00:00:47,164
New fabs are coming. SK hynix's first Yongin clean room: February next year,

13
00:00:47,184 --> 00:00:51,537
Samsung's Pyeongtaek P5 aims to start in 2028

14
00:00:51,557 --> 00:00:55,363
Profit is at a record, yet the stock is well off its high

15
00:00:55,383 --> 00:00:58,580
The market watches how fast memory prices are rising

16
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:03,890
DRAM prices were forecast to jump 90%+ in Q1; in September they rose 4% in a month

17
00:01:03,910 --> 00:01:08,499
Still rising, but slower, and the stock reacted before profits did

18
00:01:08,519 --> 00:01:14,395
